+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/AGG"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CONG"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/FPBA"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/FPHAW"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BAAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Consists largely of olivine-basalt except for a feldspar-phyric basaltic flow on Beinn Airein [NM 403 792] and an impersistent feldspar-phyric olivine-basalt on Eilean nan Each [NM 393 894]. The member occupies most of Muck, and gives rise to the strong trap topography of the island. The highest of three members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Muck."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Basalt lavas with interbedded agglomerate, conglomerate and sandstone. \r\n\r\nThe Basal Member occurs on Sanday. \r\n\r\nOn Canna, the Tighard Member, Cnoc Bhrostan Member, Carn a'Ghaill Member, Beul Lama Sgorr Member, and Eilean a'Bhàird Member are recognised. \r\n\r\nIn north-west Rum the Canna Lava Formation consists of four distinct members: the Lower Fionchra Member, Upper Fionchra Member, Guirdil Member, and Orval Member."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Aphyric basalt, basalt with sparse plagioclase phenocrysts and feldsparphyric basalts with small plagioclase crystals (<5 mm in length). The flows are generally less than 7 m thick and interbedded coarse fluviatile conglomerates are common. The highest flow on Sanday, at Creag Ard [NG 263 045] and either side of An Doirlinn [NG 266 049], contains plagioclase, olivine and possibly augite in glomeroporphyritic aggregates."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-basalt. The lowest of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-basalt with subsidiary conglomerate and trace feldspar-phyric basalt and mugearite. The second of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-basalt. The third of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL4> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-basalt. The fourth of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL5> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-basalt and trace mugearite. The fifth of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Distinctive feldspar-phyric flows include several of basaltic hawaiite composition. The highest of six members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Impersistent flows of feldspar-phyric basaltic hawaiite, basalt and mugearite. The lowest of three members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Muck."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Four flows of strongly feldspar-phyric basaltic hawaiite with labradorite phenocrysts up to 2 cm in length, which crop out intermittently all along the south coast of Muck. The second of three members of the Eigg Lava Formation (EIGL) on Muck."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BAAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Port An t-Seilich Member (PATS)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "As for formation on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Laig Member (EIGL1)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Gleann Charadail Member (EIGL2)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL4> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Glac An Dorchadois Member (EIGL3)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL5> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Brutach Dearg Member (EIGL4)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Cnoc Creagach Member (EIGL5)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "As for the formation on Muck."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Preceded by the Basal Member (EIGLB)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAgeValue> "66"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasPredominantAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BAAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 90 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "On Canna and Sanday, the succession of lavas and fluviatile deposits is over 200 m thick. It is difficult to establish an accurate thickness since faults divide the succession into a number of blocks and individual flows, groups of flows and the conglomerates show abrupt variations in thickness and continuity. The flows dip at low angles (< 3°)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) notes a thickness of > 70 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 50 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 87 - 125 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 70 - 95 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL4> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 30 - 125 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL5> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 70 - 94 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 68 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 20 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Emeleus (1997, fig. 40) shows a thickness of c. 20 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BAAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "The member is the highest part of the lava succession on Muck."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Tighard Member (CNAL2) on Canna."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Gleann Charadail Member (EIGL2)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Glac An Dorchadois Member (EIGL3)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Brutach Dearg Member (EIGL4)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL4> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Cnoc Creagach Member (EIGL5)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL5> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Cora-Bheinn Member (EIGL6)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "The member is the highest part of the lava succession on Eigg."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Port An t-Seilich Member (PATS)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Succeeded by the Beinn Airein-An Stac Member (BAAS)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAgeValue> "56"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Basalt with subsidiary agglomerate, conglomerate and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Basalt and feldspar-phyric basalt with subsidiary conglomerate and trace basaltic tuff. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGL6> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Feldspar-phyric basalt with subsidiary feldspar-phyric hawaiite and olivine-basalt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/EIGLB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Basalt, feldspar-phyric hawaiite and mugearite and trace basaltic tuff and volcaniclastic-breccia. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PATS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Feldspar-phyric hawaiite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL1> .
